            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "If the private key is missing, it\u2019s not a problem with the certificate\nprovided by the user \u2014 it\u2019s a system state issue. This should remain\nan InternalFailure.\n\nInvalidCertificateError makes sense only when the cert/key pair is invalid,\nnot when the key lookup itself fails."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Albert Lin",
                        "email": "albert_lin@jabil.com",
                        "username": "thanatoslin"
                    },
                    "message": "This is trying to fix a case that a user uploads a cert-only file without having generated a CSR first, so no privkey.pem was ever stored.\n\nThat doesn't fit `InternalFailure`. Nothing internal has broken, the BMC is in a valid state, and this is an out-of-sequence but legitimate user action, a precondition the user can fix rather than a software fault.\n\nDoes it make sense? We can pick up another sdbus error instead of `InvalidCertificateError`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed . High level Use NotAllowed for missing private key (state issue), and keep InvalidCertificateError for actual key/cert mismatch may be better approch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "This is mixing responsibilities.\n\ncheckAndAppendPrivateKey() is now doing key lookup, validation, and file\nmutation. These are install-time decisions and should be handled in the\ninstall flow, not inside a helper.\n\nWe already have install() coordinating:\n- appendKeyMap\n- compareKeys()\n\nAdding validation here breaks that separation and spreads the logic across\nmultiple places, making the flow harder to follow.\n\ncheckAndAppendPrivateKey() should remain a simple helper (append-only),\nand validation should stay in the install path."
                }
            ],
